smart-object-select bundles model files derived from the following third-party model.

Model: slimsam-50-uniform
Source: https://huggingface.co/Xenova/slimsam-50-uniform
  (ONNX conversion of https://huggingface.co/nielsr/slimsam-50-uniform for use with
  Transformers.js, published under the Xenova Hugging Face organization)
License: Apache License, Version 2.0
  https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

Files included (unmodified from the upstream repository):
  - config.json
  - preprocessor_config.json
  - onnx/vision_encoder_quantized.onnx
  - onnx/prompt_encoder_mask_decoder_quantized.onnx

Changes made:
  - No modification was made to the file contents. Only a subset of the files published
    in the upstream repository (the quantized ONNX weights and the configuration files
    actually loaded by this application) was selected and copied verbatim into
    public/models/slimsam-50-uniform/ so that smart-object-select can serve the model
    from its own origin instead of fetching it from the Hugging Face Hub at runtime.

Notes:
  - slimsam-50-uniform uses a lower pruning ratio (50%) than the existing default model
    slimsam-77-uniform (77%), trading a larger model size / slower inference for higher
    mask accuracy. It is offered as an accuracy-oriented alternative alongside the
    existing speed-oriented default (docs/adr/0005-offline-first-model-delivery.md).

